commit 0662412a3d02d0f1dedacbd7f345b40d9f91d921
Author: Trang Doan <doantranghp2000@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:16:58 2026 -0500

    ENG-1947 Use the vault's link format when dragging from discourse context

    Discourse Context entries were not draggable, so dragging one fell through
    to Chromium's native anchor drag and inserted the resolved `href="#"`
    (`app://obsidian.md/index.html#`) instead of a link to the file.

    Entries are now draggable and carry a link built by
    `fileManager.generateMarkdownLink`, which honours the vault's link-format
    setting. Two details the drop path forces:

    - The anchor's `href` is gone. Chromium fills `text/html` from an `<a href>`,
      and Obsidian converts that ahead of `text/plain`; `clearData()` does not
      remove it. `role`/`tabIndex`/`onKeyDown` keep keyboard access.
    - `text/plain` is the only slot set. Obsidian rewrites a drop carrying a URL
      into `[text/plain](text/uri-list)`.

    Verified in Obsidian over CDP with a real intercepted drag: wikilinks insert
    `[[Discourse Nodes/CLM - oy oy oy]]`, markdown links insert
    `[CLM - oy oy oy](Discourse%20Nodes/CLM%20-%20oy%20oy%20oy.md)`.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M78K284X2S2CFFM9AW2SEACF

